# game-modes-flow

## Mode Architecture
Four distinct therapeutic game modes implemented in real-world-decisions/js/game.js:

1. Standard Challenge
- Basic skill development progression
- Token-based scoring (Green: 5pts, Yellow: 3pts, Red: 1pt)
- Progressive difficulty scaling based on performance

2. Tournament Mode  
- Competitive skill reinforcement
- Multi-resident participation
- Structured round progression

3. Skill Building
- Focused competency development
- Category-specific scenario sequencing
- Custom difficulty adjustment per skill area

4. Quick Decision
- Crisis response training
- Time-pressured scenarios
- Simplified evaluation workflow

## Mode-Specific Data Flows

Each mode interfaces with scenario data (real-world-decisions/js/data.js) through:
- Difficulty level filtering
- Social skill tag matching
- Learning outcome alignment
- Therapeutic worksheet integration

Mode progression controlled by:
- Token accumulation
- Skill category completion
- Staff evaluation feedback
- Behavioral assessment results

## Cross-Mode Integration

Shared evaluation framework across modes:
1. Problem Identification
2. Options Analysis  
3. Consequence Evaluation
4. Impact Assessment
5. Decision Making
6. Action Planning

Behavioral reinforcement system tracks progress across all modes through:
- Social skill categorization
- Performance metrics
- Staff feedback integration
- Learning outcome achievement

